Intermittent, timing-dependent failure only observed under the full concurrent test suite (not reproducible in isolation): z3-4.14.1 emits an undocumented diagnostic comment line (e.g. "; :expand-definitions line: 1 position: 1") on stdout immediately after each "unsupported" response to an unrecognized option, which jSMTLIB's response parser normally strips as a standard SMT-LIB ';' comment; under concurrent solver-process load a fragment of that comment line (e.g. the word "position") occasionally leaks into the parsed response for the next command instead of being fully consumed with the first, producing a spurious mismatch against the golden -- a solver-process stream-reading race, not a defect in the test or golden
